---
import LegalLayout from '../../layouts/LegalLayout.astro';
import { site, flags } from '../../config/site';
---

<LegalLayout
  title="Cookie notice"
  description="What cookies and local storage this site uses. In short: no advertising cookies, no third-party trackers — only a small amount of local storage for dismissing a notice."
  path="/legal/cookies/"
>
  <h2>The short version</h2>
  <p>
    This website does <strong>not</strong> set advertising cookies, does not use social-media pixels, and does not load
    third-party analytics, fonts or scripts. There is nothing here that tracks you across other websites.
  </p>

  <h2>What we do use</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>Local storage (not a cookie):</strong> when you dismiss the "Windows Server 2016" notice banner, we remember
      that choice in your browser's <code>localStorage</code> so the banner does not reappear. This never leaves your
      device and is not shared with anyone.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Strictly necessary:</strong> the form uses a hidden honeypot field and basic validation to reduce spam. No
      persistent identifier is stored on your device for this.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Analytics</h2>
  <p>
    {
      flags.analyticsEnabled
        ? 'A privacy-friendly, self-hosted analytics script is currently enabled. It does not use cookies or build cross-site profiles.'
        : 'Analytics are currently disabled. If we ever enable them, they will be a privacy-friendly, self-hosted tool with no cookies and no cross-site tracking, and this notice will be updated first.'
    }
  </p>

  <h2>Your choices</h2>
  <p>
    Because we do not use tracking cookies, there is nothing to opt out of. You can clear your browser's stored site data
    at any time to reset the banner dismissal.
  </p>

  <h2>Contact</h2>
  <p>Questions? Email {site.email} or see our <a href="/legal/privacy/">Privacy Policy</a>.</p>
</LegalLayout>
